<title>POLAND: POLISH PZM FIRM SHIPPED 6.2 MLN TONNES IN Q1.</title>
<headline>POLISH PZM FIRM SHIPPED 6.2 MLN TONNES IN Q1.</headline>
<dateline>GDANSK, Poland 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's state-owned marchant fleet Polska Zegluga Morska shipped 6.2 million tonnes of cargo in the first quarter of 1997, against 6.1 million tonnes in the same period of last year, the firm's spokesman said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Krzysztof Gogol told Reuters that the company shipped 389,000 tonnes of Polish cargo, compared with 480,000 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>PZM shipped 25 million tonnes of cargo in the whole 1996.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
